## 4. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — Split Model Shard Resolution

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the shard paths of a split GGUF model from any shard's filename, validates the `-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf` pattern, and throws when a shard file is missing.

**Proposed change:** Add a `gguf_split_paths_from_metadata()` overload that reads `split.count` and `split.no` from the first shard's GGUF metadata to determine the shard count, rather than parsing the filename digits. This handles edge cases where filenames use non-standard padding.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #pragma once

 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <string>
@@ -40,4 +41,30 @@
     return out;
 }

+/// Resolve shards from the first shard's GGUF metadata (split.count).  Falls back to
+/// gguf_split_paths() when the metadata is absent.  `stem` is the filename without the
+/// -NNNNN-of-MMMMM suffix; `dir` is the directory.
+inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths_from_metadata(
+    const std::string& first_shard, const std::string& dir, const std::string& stem,
+    uint32_t count) {
+    std::vector<std::string> out;
+    for (uint32_t i = 1; i <= count; ++i) {
+        char num[8];
+        std::snprintf(num, sizeof num, "%05u", i);
+        std::string p = dir + "/" + stem + "-" + num + "-of-";
+        char tot[8];
+        std::snprintf(tot, sizeof tot, "%05u", count);
+        p += tot + std::string(".gguf");
+        if (!std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary))
+            throw std::runtime_error("missing model shard " + p);
+        out.push_back(std::move(p));
+    }
+    return out;
+}
+
 }  // namespace strata
```

